# Development

## Do

- Use `.env.example` and local `.env` for secrets; keep AI analysis in Cursor import flows (`generatedBy: cursor-agent`).
- Use hooks and API guardrails as enforcement backstop when agents edit files.
- Follow child-repo test rules when editing `repos/retro-api/` or `repos/retro-web/`.

## Do not

- Commit `.env`, OAuth keys, credential files, or generated `.cursor/mcp.json`.
- Call external LLM APIs from `retro-api` at runtime.
- Use a database, React, or TypeScript in v1.
- Run `git push --force` to `main` or `master`.
- Delete or skip tests to pass CI (see `repos/retro-api/.cursor/rules/testing.mdc` for API test matrix).
